+### Unit 5B persistence review consequences
+
+The following current-state findings refine the existing partial/drift status; they do not change the target contracts owned by the linked architecture documents:
+
+- `SF-1.2` / `SF-2.1`: Account creation still requires a caller-provided tenant and writes an admission-enabled membership, while legacy defaults/backfill fabricated tenant membership. Global registration plus explicit `JoinPublicProductionMembership` remains unimplemented; retained-data disposition or mapping and focused proof are required before migration cleanup. See [Account Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/account-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-1.2` / `SF-2.1`: Entity runtime-instance cleanup still deletes item/container families by `(tenantId, gameInstanceId)` without namespace/scope/holder closure or proven S3 classification. Cleanup acknowledgement remains unsafe until owner-local fencing, classification, and proof converge. See [Entity Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/entity-management-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-2.1`: World’s historical `world_event` replacement has no recorded retained-row mapping/backfill evidence, and legacy tenant/version column migrations use sentinel defaults without hierarchy/version-graph evidence. No recovery is implied for already-dropped rows; affected retained data requires explicit disposition/mapping or a verified no-data boundary, with future remediation and proof tracked in [World Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/world-management-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-1.5` / `SF-2.4`: `common-saga` dependency and migration-location wiring is broad through base service conventions, including services without Saga workflows. Explicit adopter selection and conformance proof remain incomplete; see [Shared Libraries](../../architecture/system-architecture-shared-libraries.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-2.1`: Game Session’s Java/nontransactional `V8__remote_followup_target_instance_effect_identity` migration is an un-inventoried exception to the SQL-only/jOOQ lineage and lacks focused exception proof. See [Game Session Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/game-session-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-1.2` / `SF-2.1`: Game Session’s live V1 `gameplay_admission_pointer` uniqueness is global `(world_slug, realm_slug)` even though pointer reads include `tenant_id`, so identical valid selector pairs collide across tenants. Focused cross-tenant selector-isolation implementation/proof remains missing; canonical `{tenantId, realmId}` uniqueness and migration order are owned by [Game Session Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/game-session-service/runtime-and-data.md#registered-durable-families-and-lifecycle-participation).
+- `SF-2.1`: Game Design’s historical `version.revision_ids` relationship was dropped before revisions were assigned to the latest tenant version, so immutable revision/version history is not proven. No recovery is implied for dropped arrays; retained-data disposition or a verified no-data boundary and future mapping/proof remediation remain open. See [Versioning & Runtime Configuration](../../architecture/system-architecture-versioning-runtime.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-2.1` / `SF-2.3`: Account’s current connect-token path is a bounded Redis map with no durable issuance-operation schema, application-encrypted response envelope, or atomic exact-request claim. The read-then-mint/unconditional-write race can produce different tokens for one live request identity, so the target exact-result and durable/fenced recovery contract remains unimplemented. Evidence is [`AccountServiceImpl.java`](../../../services/account-service/src/main/java/net/firedevops/firemud/accountservice/service/impl/AccountServiceImpl.java), [`SessionServiceImpl.java`](../../../services/account-service/src/main/java/net/firedevops/firemud/accountservice/service/session/SessionServiceImpl.java), [`AccountServiceImplTest.java`](../../../services/account-service/src/test/java/unit/net/firedevops/firemud/accountservice/service/impl/AccountServiceImplTest.java), and [`SessionServiceImplTest.java`](../../../services/account-service/src/test/java/unit/net/firedevops/firemud/accountservice/service/session/SessionServiceImplTest.java); the required Account-owned persistence shape and ADR 0163 retention declaration are defined in [Account Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/account-service/runtime-and-data.md#connect-token-issuance-persistence-and-retention).
+- `SF-2.2`: Gateway remains the semantic owner of the target replay/deny/readiness behavior, while its exact target key grammar, reset contract, catalog registration, and implementation proof are not yet converged with the canonical Redis owner documents. This remains an implementation handoff within the shared Redis work; the current Gateway marker and Account Redis map are implementation drift and must not be treated as target recovery authority.
+
+- `SF-1.2` / `SF-2.1`: Entity’s durable S1/S2 schema still lacks the target namespace identity across character, inventory, equipment, and holder/containment associations, and `item_stacks` can admit duplicate holder/item rows because its nullable-column unique index is paired with find-then-create writes. Migration, repository, and isolation/concurrency proof remain open; see [Entity Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/entity-management-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-2.1` / `SF-2.4`: The current Game Design-to-World publication handoff checks Draft state remotely before WMS commits, without a durable WMS owner-freeze row or exact Game Design `versionStateEpoch`/`publicationFence` in `ApplyWorldDesignMutation`; a mutation can race publication. The canonical target owner operations, exact identity/evidence fields, terminal outcome, rejection or drain semantics, and interleaved retry proof are defined in [World Management API Contracts](../../architecture/microservices/world-management-service/api-contracts.md#publication-freeze-and-terminal-handoff-target-state); current absence of the proto/DTO/client/persistence/handler surfaces and proof is recorded in [World Management Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/world-management-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status) and linked from [Game Design Version Control](../../architecture/microservices/game-design-service/version-control.md#publication-freeze-and-owner-handoff).
+- `SF-2.1`: Target `version_asset` and release-bundle schemas must enforce tenant-qualified version/asset referential integrity, not only tenant-scoped uniqueness plus scalar IDs. Composite foreign keys or equivalent owner-transaction/database guards and negative cross-tenant migration/readback proof remain required; see [Asset Storage](../../architecture/microservices/game-design-service/asset-storage.md#table-structure).
+- `SF-2.1` / `SF-2.3`: Automation’s `script_event_audit` and `script_work_items` uniqueness/dedupe paths omit plugin provenance and the required `bindingId` after resolution, allowing distinct plugin handlers to alias. An owner-local schema/repository migration and focused multi-handler retry/concurrency proof remain open; see [Automation Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/automation-scripting-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-2.1` / `SF-2.3`: Social’s live account-level friendship schema/API remains tenant-scoped despite the target tenant-free account-pair contract, and Social still persists guild item name/quantity value rows despite Entity-owned value authority. Global-pair migration and Entity-owned guild-storage convergence/proof remain open; see [Social Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/social-groups-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-2.1` / `SF-2.3`: Social chat duplicate-effect handling catches a unique violation inside the outer transaction and then reads in the same transaction, so PostgreSQL concurrent duplicate delivery is not a reliable replay result. Guild child writes also accept caller-supplied guild IDs without tenant-qualified resolution/composite FK protection, allowing cross-tenant or orphaned child rows. Conflict-safe replay handling, tenant-qualified guild persistence, and focused PostgreSQL/concurrency/isolation proof remain open; see [Social Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/social-groups-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+- `SF-2.1` / `SF-2.3`: Entity character updates increment `version` but update by ID alone without an old-version/tenant CAS predicate or affected-row conflict check, so concurrent progression writes can be lost. Tenant/namespace-bound CAS and focused stale/concurrent-write proof remain required; see [Entity Runtime and Data](../../architecture/microservices/entity-management-service/runtime-and-data.md#implementation-status).
+
